  bx('bl', "With Arakan and Tenasserim, Pegu made the Bay of Bengal <b>effectively a British lake</b>. Burma annexed into British India, <b>separated 1937</b> (GOI Act 1935). <b>Sindh 1843 was NOT Dalhousie 48-56's</b>: Napier under Ellenborough 42-44. His annexations: Lower Burma 1852-53, Berar 1853, Punjab 1849 + seven Lapse States."),
  tl(("1757", "Bengal"), ("1766", "Northern Sarkars"), ("1798", "SA Hyderabad"), ("1801", "Carnatic"), ("1803", "Orissa"), ("1826", "Arakan, Tenasserim"), ("1853", "Pegu: whole Bay coast in about 100 years")),
  bx('ye', "<b>Source note:</b> the board's Bay of Bengal sweep follows the curve of the coast, not strictly date order. Handout map shows only a small dot at Cachar and one unlabelled line to Assam."),
  tb(["Maritime sweep", "Steps in order"], ["Bay of Bengal (clockwise)", "1757 Bengal, 1766 Northern Sarkars, 1801 Carnatic, 1803-05 Orissa, 1824-26 and 1852-53 Burma"], ["Arabian Sea (anticlockwise)", "1668 Bombay, 1789-99 Mysore / Malabar, 1802 Gaikwad-Baroda + Peshwa SA, 1805 Travancore, 1818 Svarajya annexed, 1843 Sindh"], ["Beyond India", "1854 Treaty of Kalat, 1876 Jacobabad, 1856-57 Anglo-Persian War, 1907 Anglo-Russian Convention, 1909 Anglo-Persian Oil Co."]),
  bx('bl', "<b>Ring Fence beyond the coast:</b> every sea approach controlled by the cheapest instrument, not always annexation. <b>Self read, not MIH syllabus (teacher):</b> Balochistan, Kalat, Jacobabad, Gwadar, Persian Gulf."),
  tb(["Treaty", "Who", "Terms"], ["<b>Kalat 1854</b>", "EIC under Dalhousie 48-56; negotiated by <b>Major John Jacob</b>", "Khan of Kalat gave up foreign policy, EIC military outposts in Kalat; EIC pays Khan <b>Rs 50,000 a year</b>: reverse-SA (imperial power pays local ruler)"], ["<b>Jacobabad 1876</b>", "British State (Crown); <b>Robert Sandeman</b>; Viceroy <b>Lytton 76-80</b>", "Under <b>Subordinate Union</b> (EIC abolished 1858): permanent troops, railways and telegraphs, supreme arbitrator between Khan and Sardars; the Resident 'was now the court'"]),
  bx('bl', "<b>Makran coast</b> = State of Makran, vassal of Khan of Kalat. Kalat 1854 to 1876 mirrors all <b>565 princely States in 1858</b>: from subordinates of a company to subjects of the Crown (Ch 17, 21). <b>Gwadar:</b> Khan of Kalat gifted it to a prince of Oman <b>1783</b>; Omani enclave 170+ years; Pakistan bought it <b>1958</b>; now CPEC."),
  t("<b>Persia (never annexed)</b>", "<b>1856-57 Anglo-Persian War</b>: Bushehr and Kharg Island; <b>Treaty of Paris 1857</b>: British withdraw, Iran gives up claims to <b>Herat</b>", "<b>1907 Anglo-Russian Convention</b>: Iran divided into spheres; south Gulf coast = British", "<b>1909 Anglo-Persian Oil Company</b> (later Anglo-Iranian, today's BP): economic control of the coast", "Handout: economic imperialism at its most efficient: control resource, control coast, no colony cost", w=22),
  sec("DALHOUSIE 48-56 AS MODERNISER " + P('2013'), 'b'),
  bx('bl', "Followed <b>Utilitarianism (James Mill)</b>: reform through laws by a strong State. Built the <b>skeleton of modern India's communication and administrative framework</b> for troops, cheaper administration, raw materials, markets. Board: this is where 'future syllabus' items land."),
  tb(["#", "Item", "Remember"], ["1", "<b>Railways 1853</b>", "Army first; first line <b>Bombay-Thane 1853</b> (21 miles); by 1856 <b>Calcutta-Raniganj</b> (coal) and <b>Madras-Arakkonam</b>; board: West 1853, East and South by 1856"], ["2", "<b>Telegraph 1853</b>", "Department set up; <b>about 4,000 miles</b>"], ["3", "<b>Post Office Act 1854</b>", "Uniform <b>half-anna (2 paise)</b> rate, Peshawar to Calcutta"], ["4", "<b>PWD</b>", "Made civilian (from military); <b>GT Road</b> restored; canals, bridges"], ["5", "<b>Wood's Despatch 1854</b>", "<b>'Magna Carta of Indian Education'</b>: vernacular elementary schools, universities, education administration"], ["6", "Vernacular push", "Utilitarian: Bengal and Bihar; technical education; efficient labour, consumers, cheaper administration"], ["7", "Female education", "<b>J.E. Drinkwater Bethune</b> (Law Member) opened <b>Bethune School, Calcutta, 1849</b>: first successful secular girls' school (Phules' Pune school, <b>1 Jan 1848</b>, is the first overall)"], ["8", "Widow remarriage", "Supported <b>Vidyasagar</b> (Principal Sanskrit College 1851, Inspector of Schools 1856) and the <b>Hindu Widow Remarriage Act 1856</b>"], ["9", "Universities", "Groundwork only: <b>Bombay, Madras, Calcutta est. 1857 under Canning 56-62</b>; also Roorkee Engineering College; Director of Education (province), Inspector (district)"]),
  bx('ye', "<b>Source notes:</b> Telegraph 1853 (board stress) vs flowchart 1854: use <b>1853</b>. Widow Remarriage Act passed after Dalhousie 48-56 left (Canning 56-62). Flowchart extras: Ganges Canal, port reform for steamships. Universities and Wood's Despatch detail = Ch 19. Infrastructure outlasted its purpose: India built a nation on it."),
  bx('gr', "<b>Mains 2013 frame:</b> intro ~25 words (infrastructure built for colonial ends outlasted them) → body 4-5: railways 1853, telegraph 1853 (4,000 miles), Post Office Act 1854, PWD/GT Road/canals, Wood's Despatch 1854, universities 1857 (groundwork his) → add colonial purpose → close ~25 words. <b>Strongest anchor: Wood's Despatch.</b>"),
  sec("THE FIVE-POLICY ARC 1600-1858", 'r'),
  bx('pk', "<b>MMP: '1 Q' expected from this part.</b> Teacher: aggression rises box by box; army grew from Plassey plunder, subsidy (SA) and revenue of annexed land. <b>PoIR:</b> puppet Nawab + British Resident + Resident controls puppet."),
  fl(["Relative Isolation until 1813", "PoIR + PoRF from 1765", "PoSA 1798-1858", "Paramountcy 1813-58", "Subordinate Union 1858-1947"], "Five policies (handout dates)", 5),
  t("<b>Relative Isolation</b>", "Trade first; army small (proof: <b>Child's War 1686-90</b>); 'relative' = not absolute (not 100%)", "Interfered temporarily when an opportunity came: <b>Surat 1775</b>, <b>Salbai 1782</b> alliance, <b>Allahabad 1765</b> after Buxar (Shuja 54-75, Shah Alam II 60-06, Qasim 60-63)", "<b>Purandhar 1776</b>: Hastings 73-85 wanted to settle commercially", "Power rose after 1757 so interference rose: 'no interference' → Paramountcy by 1813", w=22),
  bx('bl', "<b>Geopolitics rule (handout):</b> States behave in line with their power; weak invoke ethics, strong choose national interest first. India: yesterday NAM, today partly NAM, tomorrow 'we should interfere'."),
  tb(["Policy", "Definition", "Examples"], ["<b>PoIR</b>", "Resident in court controls administration without annexation", "Bengal by 1772, Delhi 1803, Travancore by 1809, Satara by 1818, Punjab 1846, Awadh by 1855"], ["<b>PoRF</b>", "Military alliance with frontier State as buffer", "Awadh (ToA 1765), Hyderabad (1766), Mysore (Madras 1769), Marathas (Salbai 1782), Sikhs (Amritsar 1809)"]),
  t("<b>PoSA 1798-1858</b>", "Rulers junior partners: EIC takes <b>foreign policy + military</b>, funded by subsidy; promises non-interference inside", "Promise broken by <b>illegal PoIR</b>: Bassein 1802, Resident <b>Mountstuart Elphinstone</b> bypassed the Peshwa: 'creeping PoIR'", "1817 war was a ruler shaking off promised non-interference: <b>no powers, all the blame</b> (as Awadh 1856)", w=22),
  t("<b>Paramountcy 1813-58</b>", "Francis Hastings 13-23: EIC formally <b>paramount</b>; interfere and annex if needed; States have no rights if British interests demand", "<b>Diplomatic isolation</b>: no talks or alliance with any State without the EIC as gatekeeper (sealed bubble)", "<b>PoP = PoSA minus the rights of the Indian State</b>", w=22),
  t("<b>Subordinate Union 1858-1947</b>", "EIC abolished; <b>Crown</b> direct; rulers legally part of the Empire; <b>Prince, not King</b> (son of the King = British monarch)", "External functions (<b>Defence, Communications, Foreign Affairs</b>) with Crown; <b>domestic</b> with Prince", "<b>= Paramountcy + sovereignty formally with the Crown</b>; India = British India + 565 princely States", "Under SA same split but ruler kept <b>symbolic sovereignty</b>", w=22),
  tl(("1600", "trading company, left alone"), ("1765", "alliance partner (PoIR, PoRF)"), ("1798", "controls neighbours' armies (PoSA)"), ("1813", "declares all others subservient (PoP)"), ("1858", "Crown absorbs 565 princes (Subordinate Union)")),
  bx('ye', "<b>Source conflict (phase dates):</b> flowchart: Relative Isolation pre-1757, PoIR + PoRF 1757-1813, PoSA 1798-1818, Paramountcy 1813-57, Subordinate Union post-1857. Handout: Isolation till 1813, PoSA 1798-1858, Paramountcy 1813-58, Subordinate Union 1858-1947. <b>Use the handout</b>; know the flowchart exists. Board puts ToA 1765 inside isolation. 'Prince' after 1858, 'King' before."),
  bx('gr', "<b>Why 1857 came when it did:</b> each stage built legally and institutionally on the last."),
