  tb(["1857 leader", "Grievance"], ["<b>Rani Lakshmibai</b> of Jhansi", "Lapse 1854"], ["<b>Nana Sahib</b>", "Bajirao II 96-18's pension refused 1851"], ["<b>Bahadur Shah Zafar 37-57</b>", "last Mughal, titular dignity Dalhousie 48-56 sought to end"]),
  bx('bl', "Also joined: <b>Awadh court</b>, <b>disbanded Sikh soldiery</b>, dispossessed <b>talukdars</b>, <b>inam-holders</b> of the Inam Commission 1852 (Ch 21). <b>Canning 56-62</b> inherited the empire and the revolt. <b>GOI Act 1858</b> abolished the Company State; <b>Queen Victoria's Proclamation 1858 ended Lapse</b>, pledged respect for rulers' treaties and rights. Paramountcy became Subordinate Union; <b>no further annexations</b> (even Lytton 76-80, despite Jacobabad 1876). Empire complete: it only needed managing."),
  bx('ye', "<b>Cross-listed in the bank under this chapter (belong to Ch 19 and others):</b> Prelims 1998 pre-1857 chronology (Indigo, Santhal, Deccan, Sepoy), 1996 education sequences, 1998 Primary Education Bill 1911, 2002 and 2018 Wood's Despatch 1854, 2020 Industrial Revolution (handicrafts ruined)."),
